1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:09,950
Slide 25 breaks down "GMAIL PARSING & CONTEXT EXTRACTION." James, what is the biggest technical problem with raw emails?

2
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:14,158
Raw emails are disgusting HTML garbage, Sarah!

3
00:00:14,158 --> 00:00:23,578
A single 2-line message often contains 40 lines of tracking pixels, CSS style blocks, nested disclaimers, and 15 forwarded replies!

4
00:00:23,578 --> 00:00:29,620
If you feed that raw HTML to an LLM, you waste 85% of your tokens on marketing junk!

5
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:40,840
Look at Step 1 on screen: our ingestion engine strips HTML tags, cleans signature disclaimers, and de-duplicates nested thread replies into clean markdown.

6
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:50,620
Step 2: Gemini Flash classifies the message into Priority P1 urgent down to P4 low, extracting explicit action deadlines and dollar amounts.

7
00:00:51,520 --> 00:01:00,590
And Step 3: For every actionable email, the avatar drafts a polite, contextually perfect response directly in your Gmail Drafts folder!

8
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:10,660
You open your inbox in the morning, review 10 pre-staged drafts, click Send on nine of them, tweak one sentence, and clear your entire inbox in 90 seconds!

9
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:18,740
Email triage shifts from an exhausting writing marathon into a rapid 90-second executive sign-off.

